    <!-- Privacy -->
    <string name="privacy_title">Privacy Policy</string>
    <string name="privacy_body">Your privacy matters to us.\n\n• All prescriptions, photos, and drug data are stored locally on your device by default.\n• Photos are sent to the secure analysis backend only when you run an analysis, and they are used only to produce the extraction result — they are not sold or shared with third parties.\n• Optional cloud backup (Firebase) is encrypted in transit and stored in your own private storage.\n• The app does not contain advertising or tracking SDKs.\n• Authentication data (when Firebase is enabled) is managed by Firebase Authentication and subject to Google\'s privacy policy.\n• You can delete any record at any time from within the app; deleting a prescription also deletes its local image.\n\nFor privacy questions, contact us through the Technical Support screen.</string>

    <!-- Terms -->
    <string name="terms_title">Terms &amp; Medical Disclaimer</string>
    <string name="terms_body">Terms of use and medical disclaimer\n\n• Prescription Pharmacist is a decision-SUPPORT tool for licensed pharmacists. It does not replace professional clinical judgment.\n• AI extraction results may be incomplete or incorrect. Every result must be reviewed and confirmed by a licensed pharmacist before use.\n• The developer is not responsible for any dispensing errors resulting from reliance on unconfirmed AI output.\n• The AI assistant provides informational answers only and is not medical advice.\n• Drug information from the openFDA database is provided by the U.S. FDA and may not reflect local availability or guidelines.\n• By using this app you agree that the final responsibility for any dispensing decision rests with the supervising pharmacist.\n\nIf you do not agree with these terms, please stop using the application.</string>

